WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.868 --> 00:00:03.033
-The Supreme Court ruled

00:00:03.033 --> 00:00:04.434
that South Carolina senator
Lindsey Graham

00:00:04.434 --> 00:00:06.467
must testify
in front of a grand jury

00:00:06.467 --> 00:00:08.734
as part of an investigation
into Donald Trump's attempt

00:00:08.734 --> 00:00:12.100
to steal votes in Georgia
after the 2020 election.

00:00:12.100 --> 00:00:14.000
And yet pro-Trump
election deniers

00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:16.434
remain undeterred
as the midterms approach.

00:00:16.434 --> 00:00:18.000
MyPillow CEO Mike Lindell

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:21.534
even claimed he had access to
voting machines to detect fraud.

00:00:21.534 --> 00:00:23.834
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:23.834 --> 00:00:25.934
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:27.734 --> 00:00:30.334
You may recall that as part
of the GOP attempt

00:00:30.334 --> 00:00:32.334
to overthrow
the election results in 2020,

00:00:32.334 --> 00:00:33.567
Donald Trump called

00:00:33.567 --> 00:00:35.968
Georgia Secretary of State
Brad Raffensperger

00:00:35.968 --> 00:00:39.734
to magically find enough votes
to overturn the results

00:00:39.734 --> 00:00:41.167
in a now-infamous phone call.

00:00:41.167 --> 00:00:43.300
In his own separate call
with Raffensperger,

00:00:43.300 --> 00:00:44.801
Graham asked him
if he had the power

00:00:44.801 --> 00:00:47.100
to throw out
legally cast ballots.

00:00:47.100 --> 00:00:49.167
At the time when the call
was first reported,

00:00:49.167 --> 00:00:51.968
Graham described it
as an innocent conversation

00:00:51.968 --> 00:00:53.601
and said he was just curious

00:00:53.601 --> 00:00:56.000
about how mail voting
works in Georgia.

00:00:56.000 --> 00:00:58.067
-What I'm very
concerned about is

00:00:58.067 --> 00:01:00.767
that if you're gonna continue
to vote by mail

00:01:00.767 --> 00:01:03.400
that we need to know what
systems work and what don't.

00:01:03.400 --> 00:01:05.267
It's up to the people
of Georgia.

00:01:05.267 --> 00:01:07.167
But I think I have every right
in the world to reach out

00:01:07.167 --> 00:01:08.534
and say, "How does it work?"

00:01:08.534 --> 00:01:10.367
-That's right --
He was just curious

00:01:10.367 --> 00:01:11.667
about how mail voting works.

00:01:11.667 --> 00:01:13.801
So instead of Googling it
or hopping on a bike

00:01:13.801 --> 00:01:15.801
and pedaling down
to the town library,

00:01:15.801 --> 00:01:17.901
he decided to call
an election official

00:01:17.901 --> 00:01:20.133
right as the president
he supported was in the midst

00:01:20.133 --> 00:01:22.000
of orchestrating a coup
to stay in power.

00:01:22.000 --> 00:01:24.968
It's just
an innocent coincidence.

00:01:24.968 --> 00:01:27.467
It's like how when I want to
check if my Internet is working,

00:01:27.467 --> 00:01:29.901
I'll Google, "Is it bad that
I put my kids' college fund

00:01:29.901 --> 00:01:31.000
into Bitcoin?"

00:01:31.000 --> 00:01:32.400
It's a test.

00:01:32.400 --> 00:01:36.634
I didn't actually do it, honey.

00:01:36.634 --> 00:01:40.400
And also, if I did,
markets are fluid, so...

00:01:40.400 --> 00:01:42.801
Graham makes it sound like
he hosts one of those podcasts

00:01:42.801 --> 00:01:45.133
like "Radiolab"
or "Stuff You Should Know,"

00:01:45.133 --> 00:01:46.834
where they investigate
everyday mysteries.

00:01:46.834 --> 00:01:48.601
[ As Graham ] On today's episode
of "Tele-Graham,"

00:01:48.601 --> 00:01:50.667
we investigate mail-in voting.

00:01:50.667 --> 00:01:53.567
But first, this episode
is brought to you by Mailchimp,

00:01:53.567 --> 00:01:55.534
which is what my mee-maw
used to tell me

00:01:55.534 --> 00:01:58.701
I was gonna be when I grew up.

00:01:58.701 --> 00:02:00.701
She said, "You ain't never
gonna be a senator.

00:02:00.701 --> 00:02:03.033
You're gonna be working at the
post office as a mail chimp."

00:02:03.033 --> 00:02:06.567
And I said, "That's not
even a job, Mee-Maw."

00:02:06.567 --> 00:02:09.067
She said, "Well, they're gonna
make an exception for you,"

00:02:09.067 --> 00:02:10.501
and I yell, "Why don't you stop

00:02:10.501 --> 00:02:13.734
putting your carpal tunnel
sleeve in the dishwasher?"

00:02:13.734 --> 00:02:16.133
[ Laughter ]

00:02:18.901 --> 00:02:20.968
[ Normal voice ] Well, anyway,
if the explanation

00:02:20.968 --> 00:02:22.701
was as innocent
as Graham made it sound,

00:02:22.701 --> 00:02:24.133
then you'd think
he'd have no problem

00:02:24.133 --> 00:02:26.467
explaining that to
the Fulton County DA's office,

00:02:26.467 --> 00:02:27.834
which is investigating attempts

00:02:27.834 --> 00:02:29.167
to interfere
in Georgia's election

00:02:29.167 --> 00:02:31.534
and subpoenaed Graham
as part of that investigation.

00:02:31.534 --> 00:02:34.501
Graham sued to block
the DA's request for testimony

00:02:34.501 --> 00:02:36.200
and took his case all the way
to the Supreme Court,

00:02:36.200 --> 00:02:39.467
which yesterday denied Graham's
bid to block the subpoena.

00:02:39.467 --> 00:02:41.234
-This just in --
The Supreme Court

00:02:41.234 --> 00:02:43.834
rejected Senator
Lindsey Graham's attempt

00:02:43.834 --> 00:02:46.234
to block the subpoena
forcing him to testify

00:02:46.234 --> 00:02:48.667
in the 2020 election
investigation in Georgia.

00:02:48.667 --> 00:02:50.868
-A district attorney in Georgia
had wanted Senator Graham

00:02:50.868 --> 00:02:52.734
to appear to give his testimony

00:02:52.734 --> 00:02:55.100
before that grand jury
November 17th.

00:02:55.100 --> 00:02:56.400
Now the Supreme Court is saying,

00:02:56.400 --> 00:02:58.334
you know, "We are not gonna
get you out of that."

00:02:58.334 --> 00:03:00.567
-Damn, he couldn't even
get his bro Brett Kavanaugh

00:03:00.567 --> 00:03:01.601
to help him out.

00:03:01.601 --> 00:03:05.100
You guys remember
the sneer brothers.

00:03:05.100 --> 00:03:06.367
That picture reminds me

00:03:06.367 --> 00:03:08.300
of knocking on the screen door
at my aunt's house

00:03:08.300 --> 00:03:10.200
and getting growled out
by her two Chihuahuas

00:03:10.200 --> 00:03:13.167
while she took forever
to let me in.

00:03:13.167 --> 00:03:14.968
Looked like a couple of actors
auditioning

00:03:14.968 --> 00:03:17.734
for the role of the principal in
a gritty "Ferris Bueller" reboot

00:03:17.734 --> 00:03:20.501
where the principal
tries to murder Ferris.

00:03:20.501 --> 00:03:22.334
"You've stolen
your last Ferrari, Bueller."

00:03:22.334 --> 00:03:23.601
And then Ferris would
say something like,

00:03:23.601 --> 00:03:25.234
"You think you can kill me
and get away with it?"

00:03:25.234 --> 00:03:26.300
And the principal would be like,

00:03:26.300 --> 00:03:29.033
"I have two words
for you, Bueller."

00:03:29.033 --> 00:03:32.133
-♪ Oh, yeah ♪

00:03:32.133 --> 00:03:35.400
-We're referencing
the movies kids watch.

00:03:35.400 --> 00:03:37.634
[ Laughter ]

00:03:39.868 --> 00:03:43.934
Look for that gritty reboot
next year on Paramount Minus.

00:03:43.934 --> 00:03:45.701
[ Laughter ]

00:03:45.701 --> 00:03:47.734
So Graham will have to testify
to a grand jury

00:03:47.734 --> 00:03:49.067
about his attempts
to help Donald Trump

00:03:49.067 --> 00:03:50.400
overturn the 2020 election.

00:03:50.400 --> 00:03:52.634
And yet none of this
seems to be having any effect

00:03:52.634 --> 00:03:54.334
on Republican candidates
and officials.

00:03:54.334 --> 00:03:57.467
They aren't deterred
by investigations into 2020.

00:03:57.467 --> 00:03:59.367
Hundreds of Republicans
on midterm ballots

00:03:59.367 --> 00:04:01.734
across the country, including
candidates for governor

00:04:01.734 --> 00:04:03.968
in key swing states
like Arizona and Pennsylvania,

00:04:03.968 --> 00:04:07.033
continue to insist the 2020
election was stolen from Trump.

00:04:07.033 --> 00:04:09.534
And if they win,
they've made it very clear

00:04:09.534 --> 00:04:10.968
that they will do
everything in their power

00:04:10.968 --> 00:04:13.167
to rig future elections to
prevent Democrats from winning.

00:04:13.167 --> 00:04:15.000
In fact, many,
including Trump himself,

00:04:15.000 --> 00:04:17.501
are already preparing to claim
next week's midterms are rigged

00:04:17.501 --> 00:04:18.567
if they lose.

00:04:18.567 --> 00:04:20.300
"Rolling Stone"
has already reported

00:04:20.300 --> 00:04:22.734
that Trump himself plans
to challenge the 2022 elections.

00:04:41.868 --> 00:04:44.734
Oh, is Donald Trump
planning a media blitz?

00:04:44.734 --> 00:04:47.300
His whole life has been
a media blitz.

00:04:47.300 --> 00:04:50.434
Without the media, he'd be
selling illegal cigarettes

00:04:50.434 --> 00:04:53.734
out of the back
of a Queens bowling alley.

00:04:53.734 --> 00:04:55.601
How would a media blitz
look any different

00:04:55.601 --> 00:04:57.033
from his current strategy
of appearing

00:04:57.033 --> 00:04:59.901
on literally any right-wing
TV network or podcast,

00:04:59.901 --> 00:05:02.100
as long as it has the words
"real," "patriot,"

00:05:02.100 --> 00:05:03.100
or "America" in it?

00:05:03.100 --> 00:05:04.334
This is a man who,
let's not forget,

00:05:04.334 --> 00:05:05.701
basically had
a standing invitation

00:05:05.701 --> 00:05:07.801
to call in to "Fox &amp; Friends"
on a regular basis

00:05:07.801 --> 00:05:10.334
and ramble uninterrupted
for over an hour

00:05:10.334 --> 00:05:14.601
while the hosts just sat there
on the couch without moving

00:05:14.601 --> 00:05:17.200
like out-of-town tourists
who accidentally wandered

00:05:17.200 --> 00:05:21.567
into a 1970s porn theater
in Times Square.

00:05:21.567 --> 00:05:23.000
"When they said peep show,

00:05:23.000 --> 00:05:26.434
I thought they meant
the Easter candy."

00:05:26.434 --> 00:05:27.934
I will say,
Kilmeade in particular

00:05:27.934 --> 00:05:29.701
looks like a guy who wandered
into a peep show

00:05:29.701 --> 00:05:33.067
thinking he was gonna get
some free marshmallow candies.

00:05:33.067 --> 00:05:34.901
"Hello?
Does anyone work here?

00:05:34.901 --> 00:05:36.133
Oh, good.
The curtain's coming up.

00:05:36.133 --> 00:05:38.367
Hello, ma'am. I'm looking
for some candy chickens.

00:05:38.367 --> 00:05:40.033
Ma'am, can you not hear me
through the glass?

00:05:40.033 --> 00:05:42.968
Oh, my goodness.
Don't take your clothes off."

00:05:42.968 --> 00:05:44.801
Just this week,
Trump called in to some random

00:05:44.801 --> 00:05:47.634
right-wing podcast to repeat
some absolutely deranged

00:05:47.634 --> 00:05:49.567
and completely debunked
conspiracy theories

00:05:49.567 --> 00:05:50.901
about the horrific attack

00:05:50.901 --> 00:05:53.000
on Nancy Pelosi's husband,
Paul Pelosi.

00:05:53.000 --> 00:05:56.133
-It's weird things going on
in that household

00:05:56.133 --> 00:05:58.734
in the last couple of weeks.

00:05:58.734 --> 00:06:00.501
You know, probably you and I

00:06:00.501 --> 00:06:02.467
are better not talking about it,
Chris.

00:06:02.467 --> 00:06:04.367
But the glass, it seems,

00:06:04.367 --> 00:06:07.634
was broken from the inside
to the out.

00:06:07.634 --> 00:06:09.767
And, you know, that was --
so it wasn't a break-in.

00:06:09.767 --> 00:06:12.033
It was a breakout.
I don't know.

00:06:12.033 --> 00:06:14.000
You know, you hear
the same things I do.

00:06:14.000 --> 00:06:16.634
-Yeah, the 911 tape
seems to suggest

00:06:16.634 --> 00:06:19.267
that he knew
the identity of the guy.

00:06:19.267 --> 00:06:23.567
-Yeah. Yeah, that's a --
that's a lot of bad stuff.

00:06:23.567 --> 00:06:25.133
I'm not a fan of Nancy Pelosi,

00:06:25.133 --> 00:06:27.267
but what's going on there
is very sad.

00:06:27.267 --> 00:06:28.634
-No big deal, everybody.

00:06:28.634 --> 00:06:30.701
Just the former president
of the United States

00:06:30.701 --> 00:06:32.133
saying weird things
have been going on

00:06:32.133 --> 00:06:34.267
in the Pelosi household
for the last couple of weeks,

00:06:34.267 --> 00:06:37.834
which I guess he knows because
what, he's the [bleep] Watcher?

00:06:37.834 --> 00:06:39.634
[ Laughter ]

00:06:39.634 --> 00:06:42.501
You know, it takes
a real sack of [bleep]

00:06:42.501 --> 00:06:44.367
to start gaming out a way
you can make

00:06:44.367 --> 00:06:47.834
an 82-year-old attempted murder
victim the bad guy.

00:06:47.834 --> 00:06:49.534
Trump just makes [bleep] up

00:06:49.534 --> 00:06:52.601
and spreads it through
vague Mafia-style innuendo

00:06:52.601 --> 00:06:54.901
like he's in a deleted scene
from "The Sopranos."

00:06:54.901 --> 00:06:56.534
[ As Trump ]
It's very sad what's going on

00:06:56.534 --> 00:06:57.934
over at the place.

00:06:57.934 --> 00:07:01.734
Over at the place by the thing
with our friend.

00:07:01.734 --> 00:07:03.968
[ Normal voice ] And, you know,
as bad as it is sometimes,

00:07:03.968 --> 00:07:06.601
you know, I will admit I have
the urge to fight fire with fire

00:07:06.601 --> 00:07:08.000
and do the same thing to Trump.

00:07:08.000 --> 00:07:10.667
You know, just spread some
completely made-up accusation

00:07:10.667 --> 00:07:12.501
about him, like, you know,
I don't know --

00:07:12.501 --> 00:07:13.701
You didn't hear it from me,

00:07:13.701 --> 00:07:15.667
but there's some very weird
things going on

00:07:15.667 --> 00:07:17.300
in Trump's household, like...

00:07:17.300 --> 00:07:19.434
[ Laughter ]

00:07:21.400 --> 00:07:24.100
I hear his head is shrinking.
He hides it.

00:07:24.100 --> 00:07:25.968
[ Laughter ]

00:07:25.968 --> 00:07:27.501
He hides it
when he goes out in public

00:07:27.501 --> 00:07:31.033
by wearing a giant fake head
on top of his real tiny head.

00:07:31.033 --> 00:07:35.400
And look, I'm no fan of Trump,
but it's very -- it's very sad.

00:07:35.400 --> 00:07:36.634
It's very sad
what's happening.

00:07:36.634 --> 00:07:38.133
I mean, you see
the same pictures I see.

00:07:38.133 --> 00:07:40.234
Doctors, I guess they have to
fill his head up with helium

00:07:40.234 --> 00:07:43.167
before every speech
to make it look normal.

00:07:43.167 --> 00:07:44.801
And that's why his voice
gets really high sometimes,

00:07:44.801 --> 00:07:46.200
you know, like this.

00:07:46.200 --> 00:07:48.767
-[ High-pitched voice ] You
never stop fighting for America.

00:07:48.767 --> 00:07:52.567
And I will never,
ever stop fighting for you.

00:07:52.567 --> 00:07:55.334
-It's very sad. Very sad.
It's very weird.

00:07:55.334 --> 00:07:56.634
And, you guys, this has been

00:07:56.634 --> 00:07:59.400
"Seth Spreads a Baseless Rumor
About Donald Trump."

00:07:59.400 --> 00:08:02.067
Anyway, the point is,
Trump and his movement,

00:08:02.067 --> 00:08:03.767
which now includes Republicans
running in close races

00:08:03.767 --> 00:08:05.200
across country this year,

00:08:05.200 --> 00:08:07.033
are preparing to steal both
the upcoming midterm elections

00:08:07.033 --> 00:08:08.501
and eventually,
if they regain power,

00:08:08.501 --> 00:08:10.200
the presidential election
in 2024.

00:08:10.200 --> 00:08:13.100
In Arizona, armed right-wingers
inspired by the lies

00:08:13.100 --> 00:08:15.067
of Arizona's Republican
candidates for governor,

00:08:15.067 --> 00:08:17.734
Kari Lake, and secretary
of state, Mark Finchem,

00:08:17.734 --> 00:08:20.167
have been loitering
near early voting drop boxes

00:08:20.167 --> 00:08:21.334
to intimidate those voters.

00:08:21.334 --> 00:08:23.033
And "The New York Times"
just reported

00:08:23.033 --> 00:08:25.501
that MyPillow CEO Mike Lindell,

00:08:25.501 --> 00:08:28.267
whose phone was recently seized
in a Hardee's drive-through

00:08:28.267 --> 00:08:31.601
by the FBI as part
of an investigation

00:08:31.601 --> 00:08:33.467
into an illegal
voting machine breach

00:08:33.467 --> 00:08:35.501
by a pro-Trump
county clerk in Colorado,

00:08:35.501 --> 00:08:37.567
is actually using his business

00:08:37.567 --> 00:08:39.601
to fuel the election
denial movement.

00:08:39.601 --> 00:08:41.934
He's the single largest
advertiser on Fox News.

00:08:41.934 --> 00:08:44.801
He finances a large network
of right-wing media outlets,

00:08:44.801 --> 00:08:47.934
and he spent as much
as $40 million

00:08:47.934 --> 00:08:50.133
on conferences,
activist networks,

00:08:50.133 --> 00:08:53.300
a digital media platform,
legal battles and researchers

00:08:53.300 --> 00:08:54.934
that promote his theory.

00:08:54.934 --> 00:08:58.100
I'm honestly shocked
he even has $40 million

00:08:58.100 --> 00:08:59.534
to throw around
on [bleep] like this.

00:08:59.534 --> 00:09:04.300
Did nobody have a pillow
before he showed up?

00:09:04.300 --> 00:09:05.367
Did he invent them?

00:09:05.367 --> 00:09:07.634
Was everyone just laying
their head down

00:09:07.634 --> 00:09:09.868
on a cinder block every night?

00:09:09.868 --> 00:09:11.334
Then he came along and said,

00:09:11.334 --> 00:09:14.834
"Imagine if that cinder block
was just a little bit softer."

00:09:14.834 --> 00:09:16.267
I mean, I'm 48.

00:09:16.267 --> 00:09:18.734
I think I bought a new pillow
like twice in my life.

00:09:18.734 --> 00:09:20.767
But they're just flying
out the door at MyPillow

00:09:20.767 --> 00:09:24.267
because what, this guy
seems well-rested?

00:09:24.267 --> 00:09:25.868
He has the energy
of a guy being dragged

00:09:25.868 --> 00:09:27.567
out of a Buffalo Wild Wings
in Duluth

00:09:27.567 --> 00:09:29.434
for stuffing barbecue sauce
in his pockets.

00:09:29.434 --> 00:09:31.234
And who are these researchers?

00:09:31.234 --> 00:09:33.000
Are they just a bunch
of other middle-aged guys

00:09:33.000 --> 00:09:34.901
with mustaches
and Midwest accents

00:09:34.901 --> 00:09:36.601
screaming back and forth
at each other?

00:09:36.601 --> 00:09:38.801
"Mike, you're never gonna
believe what I found here.

00:09:38.801 --> 00:09:40.467
I hacked into the voting system

00:09:40.467 --> 00:09:41.801
and found
a whole bunch of fraud."

00:09:41.801 --> 00:09:42.868
"Great work, Paul.

00:09:42.868 --> 00:09:44.834
I'm still sifting
through the mail ballots,

00:09:44.834 --> 00:09:46.567
looking for signatures
that don't match.

00:09:46.567 --> 00:09:47.634
How about you, Steve?"

00:09:47.634 --> 00:09:49.400
"I'm filling my head up
with helium

00:09:49.400 --> 00:09:50.901
to keep it from deflating.

00:09:50.901 --> 00:09:53.067
I got da Trump disease."

00:09:53.067 --> 00:09:55.701
Anyway...

00:09:55.701 --> 00:09:57.701
this is a man
who had his phone taken away

00:09:57.701 --> 00:09:59.367
by the FBI
in a Hardee's drive-through,

00:09:59.367 --> 00:10:02.267
and he was an early and
prominent backer of Kari Lake,

00:10:02.267 --> 00:10:04.200
the pro-Trump candidate
who is now leading the polls

00:10:04.200 --> 00:10:05.200
for Arizona governor.

00:10:05.200 --> 00:10:06.767
And in a deranged rant
this week,

00:10:06.767 --> 00:10:09.133
Lindell even said
that he and his team

00:10:09.133 --> 00:10:12.501
would be monitoring every vote
across the country.

00:10:12.501 --> 00:10:14.601
-I'm telling everyone out there,

00:10:14.601 --> 00:10:16.868
we are watching
from every angle.

00:10:16.868 --> 00:10:20.400
There's people in every state,
every county, every precinct.

00:10:20.400 --> 00:10:22.634
We have cyber guys
watching this.

00:10:22.634 --> 00:10:24.100
I looked at a thing today.

00:10:24.100 --> 00:10:28.267
It was on my Twitter
back from November of 2020,

00:10:28.267 --> 00:10:32.100
and they showed CNN,
20,000 votes dropping right off

00:10:32.100 --> 00:10:34.968
of Donald Trump's total
in real time.

00:10:34.968 --> 00:10:37.567
You guys,
votes don't go in reverse.

00:10:37.567 --> 00:10:40.767
These are computer
manipulation algorithms.

00:10:40.767 --> 00:10:44.834
So what I'm telling you
is this election, it's all eyes.

00:10:44.834 --> 00:10:47.033
We have all the camera angles.

00:10:47.033 --> 00:10:49.000
-"We're watching
from every angle.

00:10:49.000 --> 00:10:51.300
It's all eyes.
We have all the camera angles."

00:10:51.300 --> 00:10:55.467
Somehow the MyPillow guy
has turned himself into Jigsaw.

00:10:55.467 --> 00:10:57.467
Although I'm not sure
I believe you

00:10:57.467 --> 00:11:00.300
when you say you have all eyes
and all camera angles

00:11:00.300 --> 00:11:02.234
since, you know,
you don't even have a phone.

00:11:02.234 --> 00:11:05.133
But if that's true,
it's probably not a good idea

00:11:05.133 --> 00:11:06.734
to be publicly confessing

00:11:06.734 --> 00:11:08.501
that you've somehow
hacked into voting machines

00:11:08.501 --> 00:11:10.968
when you're under
active investigation by the FBI.

00:11:10.968 --> 00:11:13.501
First they took his phone
at a Hardee's drive-through.

00:11:13.501 --> 00:11:15.734
Next, they'll probably
confiscate all his cameras

00:11:15.734 --> 00:11:18.634
while he's in line
at a Carl's Jr.

00:11:18.634 --> 00:11:22.267
[ As Lindell ] I'm never gonna
get that burger.

00:11:22.267 --> 00:11:24.767
[ Normal voice ]
But I will say,

00:11:24.767 --> 00:11:26.968
I did enjoy
his little impression

00:11:26.968 --> 00:11:30.234
of computer manipulation
algorithms, whatever those are.

00:11:30.234 --> 00:11:31.367
Can we see that again?

00:11:31.367 --> 00:11:34.601
-These are computer
manipulation algorithms.

00:11:34.601 --> 00:11:37.868
-Does he think
that's how you type?

00:11:37.868 --> 00:11:38.934
That's not how you type.

00:11:38.934 --> 00:11:41.200
That's how a 19th-century
English dandy

00:11:41.200 --> 00:11:43.234
chooses a candy
from a silver platter.

00:11:43.234 --> 00:11:45.767
"Ooh-hoo-hoo-hoo-hoo!

00:11:45.767 --> 00:11:47.567
Ohh-oh-oh

00:11:47.567 --> 00:11:49.534
Oh, a Charleston Chew.

00:11:49.534 --> 00:11:53.200
Don't mind if I do."

00:11:53.200 --> 00:11:55.033
The GOP might be talking a lot

00:11:55.033 --> 00:11:57.067
about crime or inflation
or culture war issues.

00:11:57.067 --> 00:11:58.901
But this is the beating heart
of Trumpism

00:11:58.901 --> 00:12:00.067
in the modern Republican Party.

00:12:00.067 --> 00:12:01.934
They simply do not accept
the legitimacy

00:12:01.934 --> 00:12:03.200
of elections they don't win.

00:12:03.200 --> 00:12:04.801
And if they gain power
next week,

00:12:04.801 --> 00:12:06.501
they will absolutely
use that power

00:12:06.501 --> 00:12:08.267
to rig future elections
for Trump

00:12:08.267 --> 00:12:09.701
or any other
Republican candidate.

00:12:09.701 --> 00:12:12.133
If they could,
they would look at all the votes

00:12:12.133 --> 00:12:13.534
in an election
against Donald Trump,

00:12:13.534 --> 00:12:15.567
take all the names,
and turn them into...

00:12:15.567 --> 00:12:16.801
-All eyes.

00:12:16.801 --> 00:12:18.367
-[ Laughs ]

00:12:18.367 --> 00:12:20.467
[ Laughter ]

00:12:24.567 --> 00:12:26.067
Can't win them all.

00:12:26.067 --> 00:12:27.934
This has been "A Closer Look."

00:12:31.167 --> 00:12:32.868
The midterm elections
are coming up.

00:12:32.868 --> 00:12:35.801
So to make sure that you're good
to vote in this election,

00:12:35.801 --> 00:12:38.667
visit our good friends
at headcount.org

00:12:38.667 --> 00:12:40.801
to check your voter
registration status

00:12:40.801 --> 00:12:42.634
or to register to vote.

